      <tr>
        <td><table border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
          <tr>
            <td class="main"><p align='justify'><font size='4' color='#ff6600'>Warning!</font></p>
<p align='justify'>Be sure that your DVD reproducer can read the movies you buy. If you live in Europe, probably your reproducer is Region 2, or maybe Region 0 (Region Free), on your DVD reproducer must be a small label indicating it.</p>
<p>The DVD movies you can buy at this web can belong to different regions. A DVD's region will be shown at its description here in the web.</p>
<p>- The DVDs labeled as <strong>Region 0</strong> are Region Free DVDs, and they work on any DVD reproducer. It doesn't matter if your reproducer is Region 0, Region 1, or Region 2, you can see the DVDs labeled as Region 0 on any reproducer. Most of Killer Video's DVDs belong to this group.</p>
<p>- The DVDs labeled as <strong>Region 1</strong> belong to the american configuration. To see a Region 1 DVD, you need or a Region Free reproducer (Region 0), or a Region 1 reproducer like the ones you can buy at the United States.</p>
<p>- The DVDs labeled as <strong>Region 2</strong> belong to the European configuration. To see a Region o DVD, you need or a Region Free reproducer (Region 0), or a Region 2 reproducer like the ones you can buy at any European shop.</p>
<p>At this moment, at www.killer-video.com we don't sell movies belongin to another regions.</p>
<p><strong>NTSC/PAL</strong></p>
<p>Besides the region, the DVDs are on NTSC or PAL format. NTSC format is the American or Japanese one, and PAL format is the European one. Usually, any modern PAL (European) TV or reproducer can reproduce without problems NTSC (American) movies if they're of a compatible region, but it doesn't happen often the other way round. Region free reproducers reproduce both PAL and NTSC.</p></td>
          </tr>
        </table></td>
      </tr>
